<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive-icon foreground: the existing Fjällkompis compass mark, unmodified.

  @drawable/fjallkompis_mark is a byte-identical copy of public/icons/icon-512.png
  — the same artwork the web manifest ships — so the launcher icon, the PWA
  icon and the splash mark are literally one file. The logo is not redesigned
  and no new imagery is introduced.

  THE INSET IS NOT DECORATION. An adaptive icon's 108dp foreground is masked
  down to the central 72dp (66.7%) — whatever shape the launcher prefers, and
  Samsung's One UI uses a generous squircle. The source artwork is drawn
  edge-to-edge (the compass points reach ~92% of the square), so used raw its
  points would be sliced off. 16% on each side scales the content to ~62% of
  the canvas, comfortably inside the safe zone at every mask shape, with a
  little room left for the parallax the launcher applies on scroll.

  Kept as a drawable inset rather than five pre-scaled PNGs so there is one
  source of truth and no regeneration step to forget.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/fjallkompis_mark"
    android:inset="16%" />
